from writer_late import Writer,B,G
import json,re

w=Writer('2025-08-25'); p=w.price
NEWS={
'us_lead':('n8447','The Wall Street Journal described Powell’s Jackson Hole message as highlighting labour-market worries and opening a path to a rate cut.'),
'us_breadth':('n5290','The Financial Times reported renewed investor interest in the S&P’s “forgotten” stocks as megacap technology wobbled.'),
'eu_macro':('n3130','Bloomberg reported that ECB officials judged they could hold rates steady in September.'),
'eu_activity':('n1372','S&P Global said the August flash eurozone PMI reached a fifteen-month high, with manufacturing conditions improving for the first time since mid-2022.'),
'eu_trade':('n4120','Bloomberg reported Ursula von der Leyen defending the European Union’s trade agreement as strong, if imperfect.'),
'cn_macro':('n1558','Bloomberg’s assessment of growing bubble risks framed China’s bull run against continuing anxiety about the economy.'),
'cn_activity':('n0971','CNBC reported that China’s July retail-sales and industrial-output growth missed forecasts.'),
'cn_credit':('n0934','The Wall Street Journal reported an unexpected fall in China’s new yuan loans.'),
'cn_property':('n1016','The South China Morning Post reported that home prices continued sliding while support measures failed to shift sentiment.'),
'cn_trade':('n1241','Axios reported Scott Bessent describing the US–China trade truce as “working pretty well”.'),
'cn_new':('n1462','CNBC examined Goldman Sachs’s investment views on China’s campaign against destructive competition.'),
'jp_macro':('n4347','The Japan Times reported Ueda’s expectation that a tight labour market would keep upward pressure on wages.'),
'jp_activity':('n4320','CNBC reported that Japan’s July core inflation exceeded expectations even as it slowed, with easing rice prices contributing.'),
'au_macro':('n0157','CNBC reported Australia’s August rate cut alongside a downgraded economic-growth forecast.'),
'au_activity':('n0303','The Australian Financial Review reported former RBA governor Philip Lowe arguing that government spending had made the central bank’s job harder.'),
'pl_macro':('n4389','ING’s analysis argued that slowing Polish inflation created room for further rate cuts.'),
'pl_activity':('n4616','Bankier reported faster Polish GDP growth and identified private consumption as its main engine.'),
'pl_fiscal':('n4665','Business Insider Polska reported a rising state-budget deficit and less fiscal room for manoeuvre.'),
'pl_politics':('n4421','Notes from Poland reported President Nawrocki’s veto of legislation combining looser wind-turbine rules with a freeze in energy prices.'),
'pl_bank':('n4869','Bankier warned that the proposed bank tax would cut sector profits and hurt valuations.'),
'pl_energy':('n4430','OilPrice reported stronger Orlen quarterly EBITDA alongside faster energy-transition investment.'),
'pl_consumer':('n4873','Bankier reported Dino preparing for more store openings in its future expansion plans.'),
'pl_geo':('n4427','Notes from Poland reported plans for the Netherlands to station troops and Patriot systems in Poland.'),
'pl_new':('n4899','Bankier described the tax-driven bank selloff as the market’s worst session since April.'),
}
def n(k):
    ident,text=NEWS[k]
    return w.q(ident,text)

def macro():
    return [
    G('US','Bullish','easing optionality / broader participation',[
    ['Macro Stance',n('us_lead')+' The attractive development is the possibility that the discount rate can fall without a collapse in corporate demand. That is a different proposition from buying every business exposed to cheap funding. A policy opening raises the value of future cash flows, but it cannot manufacture customers or repair a weak balance sheet. The portfolio should move toward a broader recovery while retaining a bias toward companies able to finance themselves. Treat a stronger market as permission to rotate selectively, rather than an instruction to replace quality with the most indebted names. The constructive view rests on growth surviving the slowdown, with inflation allowing some relief.'],
    ['Rates & Curve',w.treasury()+' '+p('^GSPC',(1,20))+' '+p('^VIX',(1,))+' '+p('DX-Y.NYB',(1,))+' Lower front-end yields support the argument for easier policy; the still positive long-end yield keeps a real financing hurdle in place. The curve movement rewards banks only if credit quality remains sound and deposit costs adjust. A lower volatility index also means the cost of being wrong is less visible in daily trading, making position size more important.'],
    ['New / Most Important',n('us_breadth')+' '+p('^RUT',(1,20))+' The relative interest in smaller companies is economically useful: a recovery that depends entirely on the largest technology platforms is vulnerable to a narrow earnings disappointment. Small-company strength can broaden confidence, but the first rally is still a repricing of possibilities. Watch whether participation holds when bond yields stop falling. Sustained demand for profitable domestic businesses would support the soft-landing case; a move dominated by low-quality balance sheets would suggest that the rate narrative has outrun the earnings narrative.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Add measured exposure to profitable smaller companies and domestic cyclicals on orderly consolidation, financed by trimming concentrated duration exposure after strong rallies. Keep a core allocation to cash-generative technology rather than treating the new breadth as a reason to abandon it. Use the latest completed S&P and Russell closes as reference points for whether the broadening survives. Reduce the cyclical addition if credit-sensitive stocks roll over while Treasury yields continue falling: that combination would imply deteriorating demand rather than benign policy relief. Reassess the bullish stance if inflation prevents easier policy while margins begin weakening.']]),
    G('EU','Mixed','policy support / trade friction',[
    ['Macro Stance',n('eu_macro')+' Europe offers a valuation and financing argument, but the earnings transmission is uneven. Lower borrowing costs help domestic services, property financing and household demand before they necessarily revive export manufacturing. A trade-exposed manufacturer needs orders and pricing power as well as cheaper money. Prefer companies with a clear domestic earnings engine over businesses whose entire investment case rests on a single tariff negotiation. A regional index can advance while exporters remain under pressure, so distinguish the broad financial conditions from the particular demand faced by each sector.'],
    ['Activity & Inflation',n('eu_activity')+' '+p('^STOXX',(1,20))+' The practical test is whether better activity reaches company guidance. An improving survey can lift a multiple quickly; revenue conversion, wage costs and working-capital needs determine whether the move survives. Banks and service businesses can benefit from steadier demand even if industrial exports lag. Conversely, a sharp currency appreciation can dilute the foreign earnings of companies that otherwise appear well positioned. Keep the domestic and exporter books separate when setting risk.'],
    ['New / Most Important',n('eu_trade')+' The temptation is to price legal or political language as an immediate restoration of margins. Actual purchase orders, delivery terms and inventory decisions are slower. Companies with flexible sourcing and an ability to pass through costs deserve a premium; those with fixed costs and little bargaining power need a larger margin of safety. Negotiation headlines should therefore change scenarios and sizing before they change long-run earnings assumptions.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Hold a selective European allocation through diversified exposure and businesses with visible cash generation. Add export beta only when order commentary corroborates the policy narrative; use domestic services and well-capitalised financials to express a steadier recovery. Hedge a trade-sensitive position if currency strength and weak customer orders arrive together. The mixed stance can turn more constructive when improved activity is matched by earnings revisions, or more defensive if the financing benefit is consumed by margin pressure.']]),
    G('CN','Mixed','market momentum / demand test',[
    ['Macro Stance',n('cn_macro')+' China is a selection market: a rise in listed equities can coexist with cautious households and companies protecting cash. The important distinction is between improved willingness to own financial assets and a broad willingness to borrow, invest and spend. Those channels can reinforce each other, but they should not be assumed to move together. Prefer liquid companies with identifiable revenue engines and strong balance sheets to a blanket bet on reflation. A market supported by policy expectations can make substantial progress before demand confirms the move; that is an opportunity for staged exposure and a warning against leverage.'],
    ['PMIs & Activity',w.q('n0674','Global Times reported a lower July manufacturing PMI, citing the National Bureau of Statistics.')+' '+n('cn_activity')+' The latest monthly evidence should be read as a description of the underlying economy, not as a mechanical timing indicator for the equity index. Manufacturing surveys reflect the balance between order books, production and inventories, while consumption and services determine whether a household recovery is taking hold. A factory can increase output into weak final demand and create an inventory problem rather than better profits. For equity selection, the useful confirmation would be firmer orders alongside better pricing and collection of receivables. Until those signals align, concentrate on businesses that can defend margins without relying on a wholesale recovery in producer prices.'],
    ['Credit Impulse',n('cn_credit')+' Credit transmission is the central test of policy effectiveness. More available bank funding is helpful only when viable borrowers want to use it and when the money reaches productive activity. Refinancing an old liability can lower immediate stress without creating a new source of revenue. A convincing improvement would involve private firms funding expansion, households taking on obligations with confidence and lenders accepting risk on commercial grounds. For investors, that argues for distinguishing liquidity relief from a durable credit impulse. Financial conditions can support equities first, but companies with sound cash conversion remain the cleaner exposure while demand for new borrowing is uncertain.'],
    ['Property',n('cn_property')+' Housing matters through household wealth, local-government financing, construction employment and the collateral available to lenders. A measure that reduces a developer’s immediate cash pressure can protect completion of homes without restoring enthusiasm for new purchases. The investable distinction is between stabilising the system and reviving the old development model. Avoid treating a property headline as a uniform benefit to every bank, builder and supplier. Better sales collections, completed projects and less pressure to discount would make the stabilisation case more credible. Until then, balance-sheet resilience matters more than the cheapest valuation or the most dramatic rebound from a depressed share price.'],
    ['Fiscal, Policy & Trade',n('cn_trade')+' Policy can improve the distribution of outcomes even before it improves aggregate activity. A more predictable trade environment allows firms to plan shipments and sourcing with less precautionary cash, while targeted domestic spending can sustain particular order books. Neither channel removes competitive pressure or guarantees an attractive return on capital. The relevant beneficiaries are companies selling into funded projects, exporters with flexible supply chains and domestic leaders able to gain share without sacrificing profitability. Keep tariff-sensitive positions small enough to survive a change in negotiating language. The better expression is a collection of identifiable cash-flow opportunities rather than a single bet that every dispute is about to disappear.'],
    ['Markets & Flows',p('^HSI',(1,20))+' '+p('000001.SS',(1,20))+' '+p('ASHR',(1,20))+' '+p('KWEB',(1,20))+' '+p('CNY=X',(1,20))+' The different paths matter. Mainland equity strength can reflect local risk appetite and policy expectations, while offshore internet exposure also carries global duration and currency sensitivities. A rise in an ETF price does not establish the size or source of its subscriptions. Use the instruments for the risks they actually carry: ASHR for mainland equity exposure and KWEB for the internet earnings narrative, with currency risk kept explicit.'],
    ['New / Most Important',n('cn_new')+' The challenge for a new buyer is to avoid confusing an improving equity narrative with an unrestricted economic recovery. A strong tape can pull forward the benefit of policy and leave little room for a weak earnings update. The signal worth paying for is a company turning better demand into cash, or a policy measure reaching an identifiable customer budget. Where that link is missing, let a rally improve the entry discipline rather than weaken it. Breadth within domestic consumption and profitable private-sector businesses would be a more durable confirmation than a speculative surge in distressed property shares.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Keep a measured allocation to diversified mainland exposure and profitable internet platforms, adding in stages when earnings and price action confirm each other. Avoid turning a property rescue thesis into an unhedged claim on every cyclical balance sheet. Trim if the equity rally loses breadth while private demand and pricing remain weak; increase exposure when lending demand, household spending and corporate margins improve together. A trade setback would justify reducing export-sensitive positions before reconsidering the entire domestic allocation. ⚠ Divergence: rising share prices alongside weak willingness to borrow would show that liquidity is reaching financial assets faster than the real economy.']]),
    G('JP','Mixed','normalisation / currency discipline',[
    ['Macro Stance',n('jp_macro')+' Japan’s opportunity remains tied to an economy capable of supporting nominal growth without destabilising financing conditions. Corporate reform and stronger pricing can improve returns on capital, but currency moves still determine which earnings streams look attractive to foreign investors. A weak yen benefits the translated overseas income of an exporter while raising imported costs for domestic businesses. A stronger yen reverses some of those effects and can change the value of a foreign investor’s unhedged position. Avoid treating the currency as an incidental detail to an equity view.'],
    ['Activity & Currency',n('jp_activity')+' '+p('^N225',(1,20))+' '+p('JPY=X',(1,20))+' The stock index and the exchange rate answer different questions. Demand for Japanese shares may reflect company-level improvements, while currency strength may represent a change in the global rate outlook or financing positions. The more durable equity winners are companies whose margin improvement does not depend entirely on a favourable translation effect. Domestic wage and spending trends are therefore important complements to export orders. An exporter can report a better headline profit while the operating improvement remains modest; look for volume and pricing to corroborate the result.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Maintain exposure to Japanese companies with disciplined capital allocation, cash generation and credible margin improvement. Balance exporters with domestic beneficiaries rather than making the whole allocation a yen trade. Add when earnings resilience survives an unfavourable currency move; reduce if equity strength relies only on yen weakness while domestic spending deteriorates. For a foreign-currency portfolio, choose the hedge deliberately: an unhedged equity position and a hedged one express materially different views when interest-rate expectations shift.']]),
    G('AU','Mixed','easing support / earnings split',[
    ['Macro Stance',n('au_macro')+' Australia’s rate-sensitive economy can benefit from financing relief, but the transmission depends on household confidence, employment and bank lending discipline. Cheaper debt service improves room for discretionary spending; it does not require consumers to spend the saving immediately. Resource businesses have a separate earnings cycle driven by contract pricing, project execution and operating costs. Avoid treating a stronger domestic equity index as a single signal about both consumers and miners. The allocation should recognise that these businesses can diverge for economically sensible reasons.'],
    ['Demand & Financing',n('au_activity')+' '+p('^AXJO',(1,20))+' '+p('AUDUSD=X',(1,20))+' The exchange rate can help cushion external shocks, but it also changes import costs and the purchasing power of foreign earnings. Domestic banks deserve credit for sound underwriting and funding, rather than simply for participating in a rate-cut narrative. Miners require an asset-specific view: a copper supplier serving grids and data-centre investment is different from a business dependent on housing construction. Keep the customer and cost base visible in the thesis.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Use diversified Australian exposure selectively, with a preference for resilient funding and identifiable demand. Add domestic cyclicals when household activity confirms the financing benefit; add resource names only when their own commodity and project economics support the case. Cut the position if weaker employment and deteriorating borrower quality turn easing into a response to demand damage. Currency-sensitive exporters can provide diversification, but should not be mistaken for a direct wager on stronger domestic consumption.']]),
    G('PL','Bearish','bank risk / selective domestic demand',[
    ['Macro Stance',n('pl_macro')+' '+n('pl_activity')+' Poland offers a domestic-demand recovery argument, but the equity market has to translate that argument through sector composition, taxation and financing costs. A stronger household economy can benefit retailers and service businesses while a new fiscal burden reduces the earnings available to bank shareholders. A lower policy rate also has mixed effects: it helps borrowers, but it can compress interest income before deposit costs fully adjust. The right response is to separate the country view from the largest stocks in its index. A constructive view on household income does not require an immediate broad-market purchase when the bank earnings outlook is being repriced.'],
    ['Markets',p('PLN=X',(1,20))+' '+p('EURPLN=X',(1,20))+' '+p('EPOL',(1,20))+' '+p('ETFBW20TR.WA',(1,20))+' '+p('PKO.WA',(1,20))+' '+p('PEO.WA',(1,20))+' The contrast with stronger global risk assets is a warning that local earnings risk can dominate a favourable international discount-rate move. A dollar-denominated Poland ETF also combines equity and currency effects; its return should not be read as a pure local-stock signal. The domestic bank weakness deserves its own position limit, rather than being hidden inside a broad country allocation.'],
    ['Fiscal & Politics',n('pl_fiscal')+' '+n('pl_politics')+' Budget choices change who receives the benefit of nominal growth. A tax aimed at a profitable sector can improve a government’s revenue outlook while reducing dividends, retained capital or lending capacity in that sector. Political disagreement can also affect the timing and durability of a measure, which makes the final legal and implementation details important. The market can price a risk before the final text exists; investors should therefore demand a range of earnings outcomes rather than a single precise estimate. Do not confuse a prospective fiscal burden with a mechanical deterioration in the quality of every loan book.'],
    ['Corporate & Sectors',n('pl_bank')+' '+n('pl_energy')+' '+n('pl_consumer')+' The useful division is between regulatory exposure, operating exposure and demand exposure. Banks face funding, credit and fiscal questions; energy companies face investment budgets and policy-linked returns; consumer businesses depend on volumes, wages and the ability to protect gross margin. Orlen and PGE should not be treated as identical merely because both sit in the energy complex. KGHM’s metals exposure also differs from JSW’s coking-coal economics. For retail and software companies, operating execution can matter more than the headline direction of the country index. Prefer an identifiable margin or cash-flow improvement over a generic rotation into anything that has fallen.'],
    ['Geopolitics & Security',n('pl_geo')+' Security spending can support selected order books and employment, while also placing pressure on public finances. Those effects can coexist. The investment question is whether a company has funded contracts, delivery capacity and a realistic route to collecting cash, rather than a broad association with defence. For the currency and sovereign-risk channel, the market will care about the credibility of funding and the distribution of fiscal costs. Preserve room to hedge geopolitical shocks without assuming that every alarming headline changes the long-term earnings of all Polish businesses.'],
    ['New / Most Important',n('pl_new')+' The immediate signal is the market’s willingness to discriminate sharply between companies and sectors. Treat a severe selloff in banks as an earnings and policy event that needs its own valuation work. It can create an eventual opportunity, but a cheaper share price alone does not identify where the new earnings base will settle. Watch whether weakness spreads into businesses with little direct exposure to the fiscal issue. If those companies retain demand, margins and cash generation, the case for selective Polish exposure is stronger than the case for buying the index indiscriminately.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Underweight broad Polish bank beta until the fiscal burden and its earnings transmission become clearer. Keep a watchlist of liquid domestic-demand beneficiaries and companies with visible operating delivery, using currency exposure deliberately for foreign portfolios. A stabilisation in bank prices is a prerequisite for adding index risk, but company-level confirmation matters more than a reflexive bounce. Reduce the defensive stance when the policy range narrows and earnings estimates absorb the new burden without damage to lending. ⚠ Divergence: firmer domestic activity alongside persistent bank weakness would show that improving macro demand is being offset by the distribution of its profits.']])]

def sectors():
    rows=[
    ('XLK','Bullish',
     'Technology still deserves a core allocation, but the route to upside is shifting from unlimited enthusiasm toward proof that customers will pay for useful products. Financing relief supports valuations; contract quality, renewals and cash conversion determine which valuations deserve that support. '+p('XLK',(5,20)),
     w.q('n2521','CNBC reported an earnings beat at Palo Alto Networks and the retirement of founder Nir Zuk.')+' Cybersecurity remains a customer-budget business, even when the sales pitch involves AI. Recurring security requirements can be a more durable source of demand than experimental projects.',
     'Favour vendors able to turn an installed customer base into broader product adoption without relying on excessive discounting. The potential earnings surprise comes from selling useful additional functionality into an existing relationship. Watch contract duration, collections and sales efficiency alongside revenue growth.',
     'A platform can report impressive AI engagement while the economics remain weak for its customers. If buyers cannot demonstrate returns, procurement discipline will eventually reach the vendor. Keep the position concentrated in profitable suppliers and reduce exposure when rising bookings fail to become operating cash.'),
    ('XLC','Bullish',
     'Communication-services earnings combine advertising demand with the cost of building the next computing platform. The attractive businesses can fund investment from existing cash generation; the difficult ones need investors to accept a distant payoff before the current franchise has strengthened. '+p('XLC',(5,20)),
     w.q('n2655','Fortune contrasted Meta’s push toward superintelligence with investors’ continuing demand for advertising revenue.')+' That is the right tension to monitor: ambitious research does not remove the need for a productive commercial engine.',
     'The upside case is better conversion of user attention into transactions and advertising outcomes. A profitable advertising platform can absorb more spending than an unproven venture. Prefer evidence of improved customer returns to a simple increase in the size of the investment budget.',
     'More capital spending is not automatically bullish for the spender. If operating cash growth lags the buildout, shareholders may fund infrastructure whose benefits accrue elsewhere. Keep the exposure, but trim if investment commitments expand while the advertising engine loses momentum.'),
    ('XLF','Bullish',
     'The financial-sector setup improves when easier short rates coexist with lending demand and sound credit. A steeper curve can help maturity transformation, but deposit competition and loan losses can consume the apparent benefit. Own underwriting discipline rather than the curve in isolation. '+p('XLF',(5,20)),
     w.q('n2766','Bloomberg framed Canadian bank results as an earnings-season test after a strong share-price run.')+' That example captures a wider valuation issue: a better macro narrative raises the standard that lenders must meet when they report.',
     'The cleaner earnings opportunity is in institutions able to lower funding costs without sacrificing deposit stability, while maintaining fee income and careful credit selection. Rising lending volumes help only if the new business earns enough to compensate for risk and capital usage.',
     'Rapidly falling yields can signal a demand problem rather than a gift to banks. Reduce financial beta if deteriorating credit commentary accompanies the bond rally. A bank that protects capital through a slowdown may be the stronger investment even if its near-term loan growth looks less exciting.'),
    ('XLE','Mixed',
     'Energy exposure needs separate views on the commodity, the producer and the refiner. A geopolitical premium can lift oil while weak product margins hurt a downstream business. Prefer capital discipline and cash generation to the assumption that all energy shares benefit equally. '+p('XLE',(5,20)),
     w.q('n1348','Bloomberg reported a slump in Sinopec’s first-half profit against lower oil prices.')+' The result illustrates why a stable headline crude price is not enough to assess the earnings of an integrated group.',
     'Watch producers that can sustain operating cash flow without requiring a large commodity rally, and service businesses with contracts tied to funded activity. An earnings surprise should come from costs, execution or realised pricing, rather than from assuming a negotiated geopolitical outcome.',
     w.q('n4088','CNBC reported India and Russia seeking deeper trade ties despite US tariff threats linked to oil.')+' Trade and sanctions can redirect barrels as well as remove them. Hedge policy-sensitive exposure and reduce it if margins weaken while the geopolitical premium fades.'),
    ('XLI','Bullish',
     'Industrials offer a more concrete route into long-lived investment than a generic cyclical basket. Aircraft, defence and grid equipment can have identifiable customer budgets, but large order books still require labour, parts and disciplined contracts to become cash. '+p('XLI',(5,20)),
     w.q('n2302','Reuters reported Deere warning of a larger tariff hit after quarterly profit declined.')+' The warning matters beyond agriculture: a company can retain demand and still lose earnings when input costs and trade barriers move faster than pricing.',
     w.q('n6249','Bloomberg described large pending Chinese aircraft deals as a potential advantage for Boeing and Airbus over Comac.')+' Treat talks as optionality. The upside becomes investable as customers commit, schedules become credible and suppliers demonstrate delivery capacity.',
     'A backlog is a liability as well as an asset when fixed-price commitments meet higher costs. Prefer suppliers with pricing protection and balance-sheet flexibility. Add on execution evidence; trim where order announcements expand faster than the ability to deliver profitably.'),
    ('XLY','Mixed',
     'Discretionary spending is increasingly a company-selection exercise. Consumers can remain active while changing where they shop, which products they defer and how much value they demand. A retailer gaining transactions can outperform a competitor even if aggregate demand changes little. '+p('XLY',(5,20)),
     w.q('n2672','CNBC reported Target shares falling as the retailer appointed a new chief executive and sales declined again.')+' This is a demand and execution problem as well as a valuation problem. A low expectation does not provide protection when the operating direction remains weak.',
     w.q('n2582','CNBC reported Home Depot shares rising after it maintained its annual forecast.')+' Stable guidance can be valuable when the market fears a deterioration. Watch retailers that preserve customer relevance and inventory discipline without buying sales through aggressive markdowns.',
     'Rate relief helps financing-sensitive purchases only when household confidence survives. Avoid treating every consumer laggard as a reopening of the same trade. Buy on evidence of stabilising transactions and margins; cut the position if discounting intensifies without a corresponding improvement in demand.'),
    ('XLP','Mixed',
     'Staples provide essential demand, but their earnings still depend on the balance between volume, pricing and costs. A company can defend sales by conceding margin, or defend margin while losing customers. Neither is the same as sustainable pricing power. '+p('XLP',(5,20)),
     w.q('n2045','Yahoo Finance reported strong Costco July sales as a positive signal for its fiscal-year finish.')+' The membership and value proposition deserve attention because consumers can favour businesses that make a constrained budget feel more productive.',
     'Look for a genuine volume contribution and efficient inventory turnover rather than a headline driven entirely by higher prices. Retail scale, supplier relationships and a trusted value proposition can support earnings resilience. The upside watchlist should focus on companies that improve customer economics while protecting their own.',
     'Defensive demand does not make an expensive stock defensive at any price. If financing conditions improve and market breadth expands, investors may rotate out of safety. Keep staples for durable cash flow, and trim when valuation depends on an uninterrupted premium rather than operating progress.'),
    ('XLV','Mixed',
     'Health care requires a distinction between an attractive treatment market and an attractive share price. The medical opportunity can expand while expectations for a particular product become harder to meet. Trial results, reimbursement and patient access can move the earnings path in different directions. '+p('XLV',(5,20)),
     w.q('n6851','CNBC argued that Eli Lilly’s obesity pill remained a viable rival to Novo’s oral Wegovy even after data disappointed investors.')+' Scientific usefulness and immediate market satisfaction are different thresholds. Position size should recognise both.',
     'Prefer companies where product adoption can translate into earnings without requiring every clinical milestone to exceed optimistic assumptions. Manufacturing capacity, access and persistence matter as much as a compelling efficacy narrative. Diversify across cash-generative businesses instead of treating one therapeutic category as the entire sector.',
     'A share-price decline following useful clinical progress can create an opportunity, but only after the valuation reflects the remaining risks. Reduce exposure if commercial assumptions outrun the evidence, and avoid using a general defensive-sector label to conceal concentrated clinical or regulatory risk.'),
    ('XLB','Mixed',
     'Materials should be separated by customer and asset. Copper is an input into grids, electrical equipment and data-centre investment; that investment case is different from a broad wager on housing or industrial reflation. Mine execution and supply constraints can matter as much as end-market demand. '+p('XLB',(5,20)),
     w.q('n2768','Bloomberg reported Codelco cutting copper guidance after an accident disrupted its recovery.')+' That is a reminder that owning the metal and owning a producer are different exposures. Operational problems can offset a favourable commodity backdrop.',
     'The preferred upside is a producer delivering planned volumes with controlled costs, or a diversified supplier serving funded electrical investment. Watch whether contracts and project execution support the earnings case before extrapolating a spot-price move into a durable margin improvement.',
     'A metal rally can raise labour, equipment and project costs for miners at the same time that it improves revenue. Avoid rewarding production promises without delivery. Scale back a producer when cost inflation or project delays consume the commodity benefit, even if the long-run asset demand remains attractive.'),
    ('XLRE','Mixed',
     'Property equities benefit from lower financing pressure, but debt maturity, tenant quality and asset demand remain decisive. A lower discount rate can improve valuations while weak rents or vacancies impair the income needed to service the debt. Balance-sheet quality should lead the selection. '+p('XLRE',(5,20)),
     w.q('n6280','Business Wire carried Dream Residential REIT’s agreement to be acquired by Morgan Properties.')+' A transaction can reveal asset value, but its terms should not be assumed to apply to every property company or every balance sheet.',
     'Watch landlords with stable occupancy, manageable refinancing needs and the ability to fund maintenance without excessive dilution. The best upside comes when improving financing terms meet resilient tenant demand. Avoid relying solely on a hoped-for revaluation of assets that generate disappointing cash.',
     'Lower rates may arrive because activity is weakening. If tenants struggle just as refinancing becomes cheaper, the income effect can overwhelm the valuation benefit. Add only when property-level cash generation supports the debt structure; reduce when distributions depend on optimistic asset sales or repeated capital raising.'),
    ('XLU','Bullish',
     'Utilities offer exposure to the physical constraints behind digital investment, but regulated returns and financing determine who captures the benefit. More electricity demand requires investment before it creates distributable cash. Prefer funded projects and a credible route to customer recovery. '+p('XLU',(5,20)),
     w.q('n6251','Utility Dive reported Black Hills and Northwestern agreeing to merge with a focus on serving data centres.')+' Consolidation shows how customer demand can influence infrastructure strategy; it does not eliminate integration, financing or regulatory risk.',
     w.q('n6305','TechCrunch reported approval of gas power plants for Meta’s data-centre project, alongside local opposition.')+' Power supply, permitting and community acceptance are investment constraints. The earnings watchlist should favour businesses able to solve those constraints on commercially sound terms.',
     'Electricity demand can grow faster than shareholder returns if construction costs, funding needs or regulation absorb the benefit. Hold operators with disciplined capital plans and trim where the market prices a demand windfall before the return mechanism is clear. Contract quality is the key confirmation.'),
    ('SXAP','Bearish',
     'European autos remain exposed to a difficult combination of trade rules, product competition and high fixed costs. Financing relief can help purchases, but it cannot alone repair a weak model mix or restore pricing power. Keep exposure selective and demand evidence of operating delivery. '+p('EXV5.DE',(5,20)),
     w.q('n6424','CNBC reported Stellantis unveiling a new Jeep Cherokee as it tried to reverse sales declines.')+' A refreshed product is a possible repair mechanism, not proof that the repair has succeeded. Watch customer response and inventory before changing the earnings assumption.',
     w.q('n4096','Automotive News raised the possibility of US and EU mutual acceptance of vehicle safety and emissions standards.')+' Regulatory simplification could help, but the headline describes a possibility. Prefer manufacturers able to improve their economics under existing rules.',
     'A powerful rebound can be driven by relief without a durable recovery in profit. Avoid chasing the weakest balance sheet merely because a trade headline improves. Turn more constructive when product demand, realised pricing and cash flow improve together; otherwise use rallies to reduce structural exposure.'),
    ('SOXX','Mixed',
     'Semiconductors combine strong long-run computing demand with a demanding near-term expectations test. A customer’s larger capital budget can benefit suppliers, but revenue quality depends on delivery, product mix, export permissions and the durability of orders. Keep the demand chain visible. '+p('SOXX',(5,20)),
     w.q('n2624','Reuters reported Analog Devices forecasting upbeat results on strong industrial demand.')+' That broadens the discussion beyond the largest AI accelerator supplier. An industrial recovery would support a different earnings engine within the semiconductor complex.',
     w.q('n0510','Bloomberg reported analysts lifting Nvidia price targets ahead of its earnings report.')+' A higher target is a sign that expectations are moving; it is not a realised earnings beat. The investment case must allow for a strong result that still falls short of an increasingly demanding market.',
     'A political capital injection and a customer order are economically different events. Do not transfer the enthusiasm for one chipmaker’s financing story to every semiconductor business. Own diversified profitable exposure, hedge concentrated event risk and add when delivered results justify the valuation rather than the other way around.')]
    labels=['Narrative','Reported','EPS Upside Watch','⚡ Breaking Convention']
    return [{'key':key,'stance':stance,'parts':list(zip(labels,texts))} for key,stance,*texts in rows]

def earnings():
    return B('The market buys resilience, then asks what it costs',[
    ['Rewarded',w.q('n2582','CNBC reported Home Depot shares rising after the company maintained its full-year forecast in its quarterly report.')+' The positive reaction rewarded a credible earnings floor through a difficult environment. The useful signal is the combination of operating stability and a realistic response to costs. Investors should look for businesses that can protect customer relationships while adjusting sourcing, inventory or pricing. That is a stronger foundation than a surprise achieved through an unsustainable reduction in spending.'],
    ['Punished',w.q('n2783','Yahoo Finance reported Intuit shares tumbling despite a quarterly beat because its full-year forecast was cautious.')+' '+w.q('n2748','Yahoo Finance reported Walmart shares falling when its profit outlook missed forecasts despite faster US sales growth.')+' These reactions make the hurdle clear: the next earnings stream matters more than a backward-looking beat. A company can deliver acceptable sales and still disappoint if the profit conversion or outlook does not meet the valuation. Do not assume that operating progress automatically creates a favourable event trade.'],
    ['Pattern','The common thread is the market’s demand for visibility. A durable customer franchise earns credit when it can describe how demand becomes profit under changing costs. A fashionable growth story faces a stricter test when investors already assume a smooth expansion. That creates opportunities in stable guidance and improving execution, while increasing risk in companies where every positive result is treated as the minimum acceptable outcome. The investment decision should begin with the expectations embedded in the share price, then assess the business against that hurdle.'],
    ['Attention into EPS',w.q('n2671','Yahoo Finance described Target beating low earnings expectations even as its shares dropped.')+' Attention becomes valuable to shareholders only when it improves transactions, retention, pricing or operating efficiency. A prominent new chief executive, an AI label or a product announcement can create a tradable story without repairing the earnings base. The next useful signal is a change in the underlying economics: better customer conversion, less discounting, more productive capital or a more credible cost structure.'],
    ['Playbook','Buy demonstrated resilience at a valuation that leaves room for ordinary execution. Keep earnings-event positions smaller when targets have risen faster than the company’s demonstrated cash generation. Use hedges around concentrated binary outcomes rather than assuming a strong company must produce a strong immediate return. Add after a result when the future profit path improves and the stock retains that improvement; reduce when management’s outlook requires a recovery that current customer behaviour does not yet support.']])

def underowned():
    return [
    B('Funded electrical infrastructure beyond the AI headline',[
    ['Attention Gap',w.q('n2832','Fortune described Meta’s Louisiana investment as a template for the grid buildout.')+' The less theatrical question is which supplier can deliver a needed component, obtain a permit or connect a customer on a funded schedule. That route offers a more tangible link between digital ambition and operating revenue than a generic AI label.'],
    ['Exposure & Risk','Watch Eaton, Quanta Services and diversified utility exposure for funded electrical work. Their risks include project timing, labour availability, customer concentration and the capital needed before collection. Avoid treating every order announcement as immediate earnings, and distinguish equipment suppliers from owners that must finance long-lived assets.'],
    ['Trigger to Watch','Add when contracted work converts into deliveries, margins and cash without an outsized increase in working capital. Reduce if projects are delayed or the return mechanism becomes less attractive. The theme earns a larger weight when implementation, rather than an ever larger capital-spending promise, becomes the reason for revisions.']]),
    B('Copper supply discipline for grids and computing',[
    ['Attention Gap',w.q('n1456','S&P Global examined copper merger activity against a strong price backdrop.')+' The asset deserves analysis through the electricity-intensive projects that require it and the difficulty of supplying it efficiently. A copper position need not be a shorthand view on the entire global economy.'],
    ['Exposure & Risk','Use a diversified copper-miner basket or a carefully selected producer rather than concentrating on a single operational recovery. Mine safety, permitting, grade, labour and capital spending can dominate the result. Exposure to the commodity does not guarantee that shareholders capture its pricing benefit.'],
    ['Trigger to Watch','Look for delivery of existing production plans and funding of credible new capacity before paying for distant expansion. A producer becomes more attractive when output improves without a matching escalation in costs. Cut exposure when operational disappointments overwhelm the asset-demand thesis, even if electrical investment remains structurally appealing.']]),
    B('Industrial semiconductor demand outside the accelerator spotlight',[
    ['Attention Gap',w.q('n2624','Reuters linked Analog Devices’ upbeat outlook to strong industrial demand.')+' The market’s focus on AI accelerators can obscure businesses selling into factory equipment, vehicles and other long-lived systems. Their earnings cycle can improve for reasons different from the hyperscaler spending cycle.'],
    ['Exposure & Risk','Monitor Analog Devices and diversified semiconductor funds for exposure to improving industrial orders. Inventory corrections and customer concentration remain important risks. A broad fund reduces company risk but also brings back exposure to the larger, more crowded growth narratives.'],
    ['Trigger to Watch','Increase exposure when improving orders are accompanied by healthier inventories and better operating utilisation. Avoid a position built solely on a rebound from depressed shipments. The theme becomes more persuasive when customers replenish for actual demand rather than merely rebuild precautionary stocks.']]),
    B('Corporate execution behind the European defence allocation',[
    ['Attention Gap',w.q('n3185','Business Insider argued that defence companies were not the only potential beneficiaries of Europe’s spending push.')+' The wider opportunity sits in the suppliers and infrastructure needed to execute investment. A policy budget matters only when somebody receives an order that can be delivered profitably.'],
    ['Exposure & Risk','Use diversified European industrial exposure, with selective attention to electrical equipment, communications and logistics suppliers. Avoid buying a business solely because its description sounds strategically important. Long procurement cycles, fixed-price contracts and capacity constraints can turn an attractive demand story into disappointing cash generation.'],
    ['Trigger to Watch','Add when funded procurement reaches contracts and delivery schedules, and when suppliers show that margins survive the expansion. Trim if political ambition increases while payments or projects slip. The opportunity is stronger when commercial execution becomes visible beyond the best-known defence names.']])]

def crypto():
    return B('Ether leads the narrative; financing vehicles still need scrutiny',[
    ['Market Context',p('BTC-USD',(5,20))+' '+p('ETH-USD',(5,20))+' '+p('SOL-USD',(5,20))+' These are distinct momentum profiles. The opportunity in a stronger token is different from the opportunity in a listed company promising to own that token. A corporate vehicle adds a balance sheet, management decisions, potential dilution and a market valuation that can move independently of its assets. Keep those layers separate when choosing the instrument.'],
    ['New / Most Important',w.q('n2012','Axios reported Ether breaking its previous all-time high.')+' '+w.q('n2014','CoinDesk described an analyst’s argument that a supply shock was becoming likely as Ether rallied.')+' A supply-shock thesis can be powerful because it encourages holders to wait while new buyers chase scarcity. Its investment value still depends on the persistence of demand and the quality of liquidity. The narrative becomes fragile when financing vehicles need to issue stock or when leveraged holders need to sell into the same market. '+w.q('n2007','CoinDesk described bitcoin mining as an increasingly difficult market in which access to power was decisive.')+' That illustrates why the underlying asset’s price and an operating company’s profit can diverge.'],
    ['Playbook','For direct directional exposure, prefer an instrument whose economic link to the asset is clear and whose liquidity suits the portfolio. Add on a controlled consolidation that preserves relative strength, rather than paying any price for the latest corporate treasury announcement. Keep the satellite allocation small enough to tolerate weekend volatility and discontinuous price moves. Reduce if Ether loses its relative leadership while listed proxies continue demanding a higher valuation, or if a financing event benefits the issuer more than existing shareholders. A miner should be judged on power, costs and funding as well as on the coin price; a token treasury should be judged on asset accumulation per share, not merely the headline size of its holdings.']])

def flows():
    return B('A friendlier discount rate is an opening, not an unlimited pool of cash',[
    ['Global Liquidity',w.q('n3630','Fortune examined the role of credit in financing the AI boom and the accompanying fear of a bubble.')+' That is the central liquidity distinction: easy access to capital can accelerate productive investment, but it can also conceal how little cash a project generates for itself. Separate policy expectations from actual funding. An investor buying an existing stock improves its market price; a customer signing a contract improves a company’s potential revenue; a lender funding construction creates a claim that must be serviced. These are linked channels, but they do not have identical consequences for shareholders. The constructive market view requires financing to support activity without allowing weak projects to consume too much capital. Where operating cash remains distant, use a stricter hurdle for both valuation and position size.'],
    ['Rates & Dollar',p('DX-Y.NYB',(5,20))+' '+p('TLT',(5,20))+' '+p('HYG',(5,20))+' '+p('LQD',(5,20))+' The lower-rate narrative has support in traded prices, but bond ETFs mix income, duration and credit exposure. Their price movements should not be relabelled as a direct measure of credit spreads. A long Treasury fund is especially sensitive to the long end of the curve, which need not follow the policy rate in lockstep. Keep some duration as a portfolio stabiliser while avoiding a concentrated assumption that every maturity will rally equally. The dollar matters because it changes funding conditions and translated earnings, yet a currency decline alone does not prove that global demand is accelerating.'],
    ['Credit Check',w.q('n3612','CNBC examined a BlackRock manager’s selective opportunities in high-yield bonds.')+' Selectivity is the right word. A refinancing window can extend a company’s runway without repairing its business model, while a lower-quality borrower can appear liquid until the next funding round is needed. Favour operating cash generation, a manageable maturity schedule and a capital structure that does not require unusually favourable markets. In equities, the same discipline helps separate a rate-sensitive recovery from a financing squeeze. If high-yield prices weaken while government bonds rally, reduce the credit-sensitive equity book before assuming that easier policy will save it. That combination would warn that investors are becoming more concerned about repayment than about the cost of money.'],
    ['Equity & Fund Flows',w.q('n3436','Bloomberg reported hedge-fund inflows reaching a decade high.')+' '+w.q('n3553','CNBC reported UnitedHealth entering Goldman Sachs’s hedge-fund VIP basket.')+' These developments describe specific channels of allocation and interest; they do not mean every fund shares the same view. A popular holding can create support while new buyers are arriving and vulnerability when the thesis is challenged. Keep gross enthusiasm and net risk separate. An investor can add exposure in one area while hedging another, and a fund receiving subscriptions can still become more selective. Use reported flow information to understand potential demand and crowding, then require the company or asset to justify its place in the portfolio on operating grounds.'],
    ['Portfolio Implication','Maintain a core of companies with internally funded growth, add measured cyclical breadth and preserve a modest liquid hedge against a reversal in policy expectations. Finance the additions by reducing overlapping exposure to the same growth assumption rather than simply raising total risk. Treat listed crypto treasuries, leveraged thematic products and indebted small companies as separate financing risks even when all respond to the same favourable rate headline. Watch whether broader participation survives without another fall in yields. If credit remains resilient and company guidance stabilises, the market can support a more balanced allocation. If the bond rally becomes a warning about demand, shorten the list of positions and favour businesses whose cash generation gives them freedom to wait.']])

def anticipatory():
    return [
    B('Nvidia: a strong business faces an elevated event hurdle',[
    ['What Is Priced',w.q('n0507','Yahoo Finance examined whether to buy Nvidia before its Aug. 27 earnings report.')+' The preview puts a clear event ahead of a business already carrying high expectations. Investors need to distinguish a sound long-run demand thesis from the payoff on a position established immediately before a closely watched result.'],
    ['Conditional Expression','Retain a core position sized for ordinary volatility, but hedge concentrated event exposure. Add after the report only if delivered growth, customer demand and the future earnings path justify the valuation. If a strong result fails to hold its initial price response, let the market absorb supply before adding more.'],
    ['Risk','The main risk is paying for a result that the market already expects. Export restrictions, product transitions or customer concentration can also change the quality of future revenue. A favourable headline should not override a weaker cash-flow or demand interpretation.']]),
    B('Rate relief with growth intact, or a warning about demand',[
    ['What Is Priced',w.q('n0512','Fortune reported JPMorgan’s view that Powell remained central to the next policy move amid a divided committee.')+' The market’s constructive scenario is easier policy with a surviving earnings base. The less attractive scenario is easier policy arriving because demand and employment are weakening more severely.'],
    ['Conditional Expression','Own profitable smaller companies and selected domestic cyclicals when credit remains stable and earnings expectations hold. Pair them with liquid duration exposure. If loan quality or consumer transactions deteriorate, reduce the cyclical leg and let the defensive allocation carry more of the portfolio.'],
    ['Risk','A rate cut can be bullish or bearish depending on what makes it necessary. Do not use the policy direction as a substitute for reading company orders, wages and margins. Inflation pressure could also limit relief while leaving the demand problem unresolved.']]),
    B('Polish bank taxation: trade a range of earnings outcomes',[
    ['What Is Priced',w.q('n4431','The Wall Street Journal reported Poland planning a higher tax rate for banks.')+' The selloff reflects a prospective redistribution of profits, but the durable valuation depends on the final burden, implementation and each lender’s ability to absorb it. A large price decline does not settle those questions.'],
    ['Conditional Expression','Keep broad bank exposure light until the policy range narrows. Add selectively only when the resulting earnings base, capital needs and dividend capacity support the price. Use businesses less directly exposed to the measure for a domestic-demand position rather than buying the whole index by default.'],
    ['Risk','Political uncertainty can produce sharp relief rallies before earnings estimates stabilise. Conversely, a measure that appears manageable at sector level can affect weaker institutions more severely. Avoid assuming that a uniform tax produces an identical shareholder outcome at every bank.']]),
    B('AI adoption: customer returns become the next financing test',[
    ['What Is Priced',w.q('n5160','Axios highlighted an MIT study reporting poor returns from many organisational AI investments.')+' Treat the study as a challenge to an indiscriminate spending narrative, rather than a verdict that every product or project fails. The market will increasingly ask which applications create measurable economic value.'],
    ['Conditional Expression','Prefer vendors with renewal strength, useful products and demonstrable customer savings. Keep infrastructure exposure where contracts are funded and delivery is credible. Reduce speculative software positions if enthusiasm for adoption fails to become revenue, or if customers delay projects while reassessing their economics.'],
    ['Risk','Early implementation problems do not necessarily determine mature product economics, but they can alter the pace of spending. The danger is extrapolating a large potential market into a smooth earnings path. Conversely, dismissing all adoption because some projects disappoint can miss businesses already solving valuable problems.']])]

def catalysts():
    return [
    B('$NVDA — own the demand engine, hedge the expectation hurdle',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',w.q('n2834','Bloomberg framed Nvidia’s earnings as the major equity risk event after the Fed-driven rally.')+' Maintain a constructive long-run view on useful computing demand while acknowledging the immediate burden of expectations. The trade should survive an ordinary disappointment without forcing a sale of the core allocation.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('NVDA',(5,20))+' A positive result must sustain buying interest after the announcement. Export policy, product mix and customer concentration can complicate a simple revenue-growth interpretation.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Hold a measured core and hedge event concentration. Add on confirmed operating progress and a stable price response; trim if the valuation rises while the future profit path becomes less clear.']],stance='Bullish'),
    B('$INTC — financing support still needs an operating turnaround',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',w.q('n6737','The BBC reported a US government stake in Intel.')+' The capital relationship changes the financing and political context, but a successful investment still requires a competitive product and foundry execution. Treat support as runway, rather than as a substitute for customers.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('INTC',(1,20))+' A strong move can anticipate more operational progress than has been delivered. Political involvement also changes the range of strategic and governance outcomes.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Use a small tactical position or watchlist entry. Add only when customer commitments and operating delivery corroborate the financing story; reduce if the share response depends mainly on expectations of additional official support.']],stance='Mixed'),
    B('$PANW — a security budget with an AI opportunity',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',w.q('n2522','Reuters reported Palo Alto Networks forecasts signalling an AI boost for cybersecurity tools, with shares rising.')+' The attractive mechanism is existing customer demand meeting a broader useful product set. Security spending can offer a clearer commercial link than an experimental technology budget.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('PANW',(5,20))+' The stock still needs recurring revenue to turn into collections and durable margins. Product bundling can increase customer reach while obscuring the underlying price paid.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Buy orderly consolidation while recurring demand and cash generation hold. Reduce if contract growth requires heavier concessions or if future guidance no longer supports the valuation. Keep the position distinct from a generic wager on higher AI spending.']],stance='Bullish'),
    B('$WMT — customer strength must survive the margin hurdle',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',w.q('n2745','CNBC reported Walmart raising its sales and earnings outlook while warning that tariff costs were rising.')+' The business has a customer-value argument, but the share-price outcome depends on the profit delivered against expectations. Strong sales alone cannot guarantee an attractive entry.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('WMT',(5,20))+' Tariff pass-through, mix and operating expenses can determine how much revenue reaches shareholders. The risk is paying a resilience premium that assumes an effortless conversion into earnings.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Accumulate selectively when valuation and margin evidence align. Reduce if higher prices weaken customer demand or if costs rise faster than operating efficiencies. Prefer a measured position to using the stock as a substitute for cash.']],stance='Mixed'),
    B('$UNH — an influential buyer is a prompt for work, not the thesis',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',w.q('n5286','The Motley Fool highlighted purchases of UnitedHealth by prominent investors and asked whether others should follow.')+' The investment opportunity must rest on the company’s economics, not on the names attached to a filing. A respected buyer can draw attention without removing operating uncertainty.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('UNH',(5,20))+' A recovery position needs evidence that the earnings base and liabilities are becoming more predictable. A share rebound can move faster than that evidence.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Keep it on a disciplined recovery watchlist or hold a small position. Increase only as operating visibility improves; reduce if the thesis becomes a chain of appeals to other investors’ confidence rather than better business results.']],stance='Mixed'),
    B('$BHP — a dividend response does not erase commodity pressure',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',w.q('n0302','Reuters reported BHP’s iron-ore-driven profit decline while its dividend supported the shares.')+' The distinction is useful: capital returns can improve the investment proposition even when the commodity earnings cycle is difficult. The sustainability of those returns remains the central question.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('BHP.AX',(5,20))+' Commodity prices, project execution and the funding of new assets can constrain the cash available to shareholders. Do not capitalise an isolated payout as though it were a guaranteed annuity.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Own selectively for diversified assets and disciplined capital allocation. Add when operating cash supports investment and distributions together; reduce if shareholder returns rely on an optimistic commodity recovery or an increasingly stretched balance sheet.']],stance='Mixed')]

def retail():
    return [
    B('Opendoor / OPEN — the house-flipper becomes the next AI comeback',[
    ['Why Retail Is Here',w.q('n5257','MarketWatch described Opendoor putting its weight behind AI as the stock surged, while warning buyers to be careful.')+' This is a particularly potent retail story because it offers several emotional hooks at once: a beaten-down business, a vast familiar market, a technology reinvention and the possibility of being early to a recovery. The crowd can translate the pitch into a simple claim that software will make selling a house easier and more efficient. That simplicity is the attraction. It lets a buyer focus on the size of the opportunity rather than on the difficult economics of owning inventory, financing it and selling it at a profit. The comeback identity can become stronger than the current earnings argument.'],
    ['What Is Driving It',p('OPEN',(1,5,20))+' '+p('^RUT',(1,))+' The macro backdrop gives the story additional force. A prospect of cheaper financing makes housing-related exposure easier to imagine, while a sharp broadening rally encourages investors to revisit companies they had previously dismissed. But the layers should remain separate: a lower policy-rate expectation is not the same as a lower mortgage bill for every buyer, and a higher share price is not operating cash. The opportunity would become more durable if the technology pitch translated into better transaction economics. Until that happens, the price movement itself is doing much of the persuasion.'],
    ['The Social Signal',w.q('n5217','Bloomberg carried EMJ’s Eric Jackson describing Opendoor as a “cult” stock and discussing an exceptionally ambitious upside case.')+' That language captures the social mechanism better than a conventional valuation debate. A stock becomes a badge of belonging: believers see institutional scepticism as the reason the opportunity exists, while each rally supplies a new illustration of why the group was right to ignore it. The MarketWatch warning and the promotional framing can circulate together because they serve different audiences. One asks how the business will earn money; the other asks how large a market revaluation could become. The risk for a new entrant is mistaking widespread repetition of the second question for a satisfactory answer to the first.'],
    ['Historical Analog','The useful comparison is GameStop in 2021: a shareholder identity can become part of the product investors believe they are buying. The sequence is mechanical. A simple recovery or disruption thesis attracts an initial group, a strong price move makes the thesis visible, and new participants treat scepticism as fuel for another advance. That can sustain a trade longer than a conventional investor expects, especially when the share price is low enough to make a distant target feel psychologically attainable. The resemblance concerns the feedback loop, not a claim that the businesses or financing structures are identical. A powerful community can change trading conditions; it cannot by itself guarantee an attractive return on capital.'],
    ['Smart Money View','A professional investor can recognise a real opportunity in reducing friction around housing transactions and still decline the share price offered after a dramatic move. The central disagreement is about the speed and economics of the transformation. Software may improve matching, pricing or processing, but the business must still manage acquisition costs, inventory exposure and financing. A tactical investor may participate in momentum while hedging it; a fundamental investor needs a credible route from transactions to cash. Neither approach should be confused with a promise that a large potential market belongs to existing shareholders. The more the valuation rests on future execution, the more important it is to understand who funds that execution and what claims they receive.'],
    ['When the Narrative Breaks','The first warning is a failure to retain buying interest after favourable news. If a fresh AI or leadership announcement produces only a brief bounce, the supply of new converts may be thinning. The fundamental warning is improved activity without better unit economics or cash conversion. A financing decision that expands the share count faster than the value created for shareholders would also weaken the comeback case. A broader reversal in rate-sensitive small companies could remove the macro support just as expectations become demanding. Treat OPEN as a tightly sized speculative trade, not as a cheap substitute for diversified housing exposure. Keep a predefined exit tied to failed price strength or weaker operating delivery, and avoid increasing risk merely because the story becomes more emotionally persuasive.']]),
    B('Ether / ETH — the record makes the scarcity story feel inevitable',[
    ['Why Retail Is Here',w.q('n2013','Decrypt reported Ethereum reaching a record price in its push toward a higher round-number milestone.')+' '+p('ETH-USD',(1,20))+' The emotional attraction is the feeling that a long-standing thesis has finally become visible in the price. A token with a powerful network story and a fresh record invites holders to reinterpret every pullback as a temporary shortage of conviction. The availability of listed exposure can make the trade feel accessible to investors who would otherwise avoid direct custody.'],
    ['Where It Breaks','A scarcity argument weakens when demand slows or when investors discover that their chosen vehicle adds financing and valuation risk. The asset, an ETF and a corporate treasury company are different claims. Prefer transparent exposure, avoid borrowing against a momentum assumption and reduce if Ether loses relative strength while promotional targets become more aggressive. The important question is who will buy the next unit and why, rather than how far an attractive chart can be extended.']]),
    B('Intel / INTC — the government stake becomes a turnaround shortcut',[
    ['Why Retail Is Here',w.q('n6710','The Wall Street Journal reported Trump and Intel agreeing on a US stake, with the president pointing to more deals.')+' '+p('INTC',(1,5))+' The crowd’s shortcut is easy to understand: official involvement feels like validation and a stronger safety net. It also connects an old technology franchise to the emotionally compelling theme of national industrial renewal. That can draw buyers who would not otherwise spend time analysing process technology or foundry economics.'],
    ['Where It Breaks','Political importance and shareholder return do not have to move together. New capital can preserve strategic capacity while existing shareholders still face execution risk, dilution or unattractive returns on further investment. The turnaround becomes credible when customers, products and operating performance support it. Keep a tactical position small, demand progress beyond the financing announcement and reduce if every setback is answered only with the hope of additional official support.']]),
    B('Gold / GLD — a hedge that does not need a perfect soft landing',[
    ['Why Retail Is Here',w.q('n5272','CNBC examined a gold-related trade as investors sought a hedge against volatility and risk.')+' '+p('GC=F',(1,20))+' Gold offers a clear story when investors like equities but distrust the policy path: hold an asset that does not require a company to meet an earnings forecast. That appeal can coexist with stronger risk assets because the buyer is often purchasing insurance against a different outcome.'],
    ['Where It Breaks','The hedge still has an entry price and can suffer when the dollar strengthens, yields rise or investors sell liquid assets to meet other obligations. A mining share adds operating and cost risks that bullion does not carry. Use a measured allocation with a clear portfolio purpose; reduce if the position grows into a dominant directional bet. The defensive case is stronger when it survives ordinary fluctuations without requiring a fresh crisis headline every day.']])]

def main():
    spec={'date':w.date,'geo':macro(),'sectors':sectors(),'earnings_pattern':earnings(),'underowned':underowned(),
          'crypto':crypto(),'flows':flows(),'anticipatory':anticipatory(),'catalysts':catalysts(),
          'retail_intro':'Opendoor’s AI comeback is the clearest speculative narrative at the intersection of attention and a dramatic price move, recalling the feedback loops around GameStop in 2021, Tesla in 2020 and Nvidia in 2023.',
          'retail':retail()}
    w.save(spec)

if __name__=='__main__':main()


